4. Assumptions and constraints
The numerical policy values are proposed for the coursework. They are not confirmed
university rules.
ID Type Description
A-01 Assumption
Students may borrow up to 3 copies for 14 calendar days; faculty up
to 5 copies for 28 days. An active overdue loan prevents further
borrowing.
A-02 Assumption
Reservations use first-in, first-out order by request timestamp (ties
by reservation ID). Only active members below their current limit
and without overdue loans qualify for a hold. Proposed hold
duration: 48 hours.
A-03 Assumption
Overdue begins the day after the due date. One notice is shown
inside the LMS for each overdue loan. No fine amounts are
calculated; penalty rules are not confirmed.
C-01 Constraint
Coursework covers analysis, UML and a clickable UI, not a
complete working system. Production hosting, live messaging,
payment processing, SSO and live record migration are excluded.
C-02 Constraint Only fictional demonstration data may be used; the system design
must not expose real student, faculty or staff records.
